        osdi:TT_N36_ManA_LER ,
        osdi:TT_N36_ManA ,
        osdi:TT_N36_Disease ;
    osdi:hasDescription "N36. Acute manifestation with a frequency (2 episodes per year) and a life expectancy reduction. The tree multiplies the one-time payoffs of an acute manifestation by the expected number of episodes, but there is no reasonable semantics for its effects on the life expectancy (instant death, life expectancy reduction, increased mortality rate), so the generation of the tree must fail." .


